msgid ""
"maximum interval between keyframes in frames (default: &250 or"
"<br>\n"
"one keyframe every ten seconds in a 25fps movie). Keyframes are"
"<br>\n"
"needed for seeking as seeking is only possible to a keyframe,"
"<br>\n"
"but keyframes need more space than  other frames, so larger"
"<br>\n"
"numbers here mean slightly smaller files but less precise seeking."
"<br>\n"
"0 is equivalent to 1, which makes every frame a keyframe."
"<br>\n"
"Values >300 are not recommended as the quality might be bad"
"<br>\n"
"depending upon decoder, encoder and luck. For a strict MPEG-1/2/4"
"<br>\n"
"compliance this would have to be lt;=132"
